course: dictionary
lesson: 11794
title: Beneficial: a formal word for good
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Beneficial» is a more formal word for good or helpful. It tells you that something has a good effect on you or on something else. «Eating vegetables is beneficial to your health.» This means vegetables do good things for your body.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «The new bus route was beneficial for the whole village.» The people who gained a useful bus were the ones who were helped, so beneficial means helpful. Swap in good and the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning works.
explain: Beneficial is often followed by to or for, as in beneficial to health or beneficial for plants. Its noun is benefit, which means a good thing you gain. «Sleep has many benefits» means sleep does many good things for you.
explain: Writers use beneficial in science, health and formal writing. «Some bacteria in your gut are beneficial.» This tells you some bacteria are good for you. When a word feels too formal, use the context first, then check a dictionary if you still need to.
fact: Beneficial is an adjective. It means good for you, helpful, or having a good effect.
fact: Its formal meaning is giving an advantage or a profit.
fact: The noun is benefit: a good thing that you gain.
fact: «Mutually beneficial» means good for both sides, like a deal where both people gain.
fact: Use beneficial with to or for: «beneficial to health», «beneficial for growing».
exercise: «Eating vegetables is beneficial to your health.» What does beneficial mean here? | Expensive to buy | *Good for you | Very green in colour | Harmful to your body
exercise: «The two shops made a mutually beneficial deal, so both gained.» What does mutually beneficial mean? | *Good for both sides | Good for only one side | Done in secret | Bad for both sides
exercise: Find and copy the noun that comes from beneficial. | health | village | *benefit | bacteria
test: «Some bacteria in your gut are beneficial.» Which word is the closest synonym of beneficial? | Hidden | Harmful | Heavy | *Helpful
test: Nadia says beneficial means bad. Is she right? | Yes, it means bad for you | Not sure, it means expensive | Yes, it means the same as harmful | *No, it means good or helpful
exam: «Too much sugar is harmful, but a little fruit is beneficial.» Which word means the opposite of beneficial? | *harmful | helpful | kind | useful
